    {"name":"a letter beyond ASCII in the value of data-bind","source":"<input data-bind=\"år\">","issues":[{"code":"signal-name","start":18,"end":20,"severity":"warning","message":"data-bind declares the signal år, as written, which no $name reaches: Datastar reads only ASCII letters, digits and _ after a $, so the browser looks for a JavaScript variable instead; only the bracket form $['år'] reads it."}]},
    {"name":"a dollar in the value of data-bind, said with the signal it reads","source":"<input data-bind=\"$user\">","issues":[{"code":"signal-name","start":18,"end":23,"severity":"warning","message":"data-bind declares the signal $user, as written, which holds the $ itself, so $user does not reach it: that reads the signal user.","fixes":["<input data-bind=\"user\">"]}]},
    {"name":"__proto__ in the object form, a warning","source":"<div data-signals=\"{__proto__: {x: 1}}\"></div>","issues":[{"code":"signal-name","start":20,"end":29,"severity":"warning","message":"In an object literal __proto__ sets the object's prototype, so Datastar gets no signal from it."}]},
    {"name":"a key cut short by a template construct","source":"<div data-signals:${key}=\"1\"></div>","issues":[]},
    {"name":"data-computed values that may give a function","source":"<div data-computed=\"{a: $x ? () => 1 : () => 2, b: new Function('return 7'), c: 'a' &amp;&amp; (() => 2), d: $f, e: f`x`}\"></div><div data-computed=\"fns\"></div>","issues":[]},
    {"name":"data-computed values that give no function","source":"<div data-computed=\"{a: -1, b: 'x', c: [1], d: undefined, e: `t`, f: !$x, g: $x * 2, h: typeof $x}\"></div><div data-computed=\"'total'\"></div>","issues":[{"code":"computed-value","start":21,"end":22,"severity":"error","message":"Without a key, each value of data-computed must be a function, such as a: () => ...; Datastar raises ComputedExpectedFunction for a."},{"code":"computed-value","start":28,"end":29,"severity":"error","message":"Without a key, each value of data-computed must be a function, such as b: () => ...; Datastar raises ComputedExpectedFunction for b."},{"code":"computed-value","start":36,"end":37,"severity":"error","message":"Without a key, each value of data-computed must be a function, such as c: () => ...; Datastar raises ComputedExpectedFunction for c."},{"code":"computed-value","start":44,"end":45,"severity":"error","message":"Without a key, each value of data-computed must be a function, such as d: () => ...; Datastar raises ComputedExpectedFunction for d."},{"code":"computed-value","start":58,"end":59,"severity":"error","message":"Without a key, each value of data-computed must be a function, such as e: () => ...; Datastar raises ComputedExpectedFunction for e."},{"code":"computed-value","start":66,"end":67,"severity":"error","message":"Without a key, each value of data-computed must be a function, such as f: () => ...; Datastar raises ComputedExpectedFunction for f."},{"code":"computed-value","start":74,"end":75,"severity":"error","message":"Without a key, each value of data-computed must be a function, such as g: () => ...; Datastar raises ComputedExpectedFunction for g."},{"code":"computed-value","start":85,"end":86,"severity":"error","message":"Without a key, each value of data-computed must be a function, such as h: () => ...; Datastar raises ComputedExpectedFunction for h."},{"code":"computed-value","start":126,"end":133,"severity":"warning","message":"Without a key, data-computed takes an object of functions, such as {total: () => $a + 1}: Datastar declares no signal from this value, and raises ComputedExpectedFunction when it is a string. Name the signal in the key instead: data-computed:total."}]},
    {"name":"a pattern written as a string with slashes and no flag, which the client cuts off","source":"<pre data-json-signals=\"{include: '/^user/', exclude: '/^_/'}\"></pre><pre data-json-signals=\"{include: '/path/to/thing'}\"></pre>","issues":[]},
    {"name":"a pattern written as a string with a flag, said as the client reads it","source":"<pre data-json-signals=\"{include: '/^user/i'}\"></pre>","issues":[{"code":"filter-pattern","start":34,"end":44,"severity":"warning","message":"Datastar cuts one / from each end of a string include and takes the rest as the pattern, so /i stays in it and is matched as text, not read as flags. Write the regular expression literal /^user/i.","fixes":["<pre data-json-signals=\"{include: /^user/i}\"></pre>"]}]},
    {"name":"a pattern with a flag in json, which holds no regular expression","source":"<pre data-json-signals='{\"include\": \"/^user/g\"}'></pre>","issues":[{"code":"filter-pattern","start":36,"end":46,"severity":"warning","message":"Datastar cuts one / from each end of a string include and takes the rest as the pattern, so /g stays in it and is matched as text, not read as flags. JSON holds no regular expression: write the value as JavaScript, with the literal /^user/g."}]},
    {"name":"a pattern with a flag and an escape, which a literal would read otherwise","source":"<pre data-json-signals=\"{include: '/^a\\\\.b/i'}\"></pre>","issues":[{"code":"filter-pattern","start":34,"end":45}]},
    {"name":"a dollar in a string of a filter","source":"<pre data-json-signals=\"{include: '$x'}\"></pre>","issues":[]},
    {"name":"a flag before the duration, with a flag it does not know","source":"<button data-on:click__debounce.leading.500ms.bogus=\"$n++\"></button>","issues":[{"code":"modifier-args","start":23,"end":51,"severity":"error","message":"Datastar reads the first argument of __debounce as its duration, so with .leading first it reads none and does not wait. The duration comes first."},{"code":"modifier-args","start":23,"end":51,"severity":"error","message":"Unknown flag .bogus for __debounce. Allowed: .leading, .notrailing."}]},
    {"name":"a fraction in a duration, with a flag it does not know","source":"<button data-on:click__debounce.1.5s.bogus=\"$n++\"></button>","issues":[{"code":"modifier-args","start":23,"end":42,"severity":"error","message":"Datastar reads __debounce.1.5s as 1 ms: a dot separates arguments, so a duration has no fraction. Write __debounce.1500ms."},{"code":"modifier-args","start":23,"end":42,"severity":"error","message":"Unknown flag .bogus for __debounce. Allowed: .leading, .notrailing."}]},
    {"name":"a pattern whose last slash is escaped, a slash all the same once the string is read","source":"<pre data-json-signals=\"{include: '/^a\\/i'}\"></pre>","issues":[{"code":"filter-pattern","start":34,"end":42}]},
    {"name":"data-computed values that test a key or a class","source":"<div data-computed=\"{a: 'k' in $o, b: $p instanceof Date}\"></div>","issues":[{"code":"computed-value","start":21,"end":22},{"code":"computed-value","start":35,"end":36}]},
    {"name":"a pattern with a slash inside, which the literal escapes","source":"<pre data-json-signals=\"{include: '/a/b/i'}\"></pre>","issues":[{"code":"filter-pattern","start":34,"end":42,"severity":"warning","message":"Datastar cuts one / from each end of a string include and takes the rest as the pattern, so /i stays in it and is matched as text, not read as flags. Write the regular expression literal /a\\/b/i.","fixes":["<pre data-json-signals=\"{include: /a\\/b/i}\"></pre>"]}]},
    {"name":"a pattern with a flag given twice, or u with v, which no literal takes","source":"<pre data-json-signals=\"{include: '/^user/ii'}\"></pre><pre data-json-signals=\"{include: '/^user/uv'}\"></pre>","issues":[{"code":"filter-pattern","start":34,"end":45,"severity":"warning","message":"Datastar cuts one / from each end of a string include and takes the rest as the pattern, so /ii stays in it and is matched as text, not read as flags. As flags ii would not do either: each is given once, and u and v not together. Write a regular expression literal with the flags meant."},{"code":"filter-pattern","start":88,"end":99,"severity":"warning","message":"Datastar cuts one / from each end of a string include and takes the rest as the pattern, so /uv stays in it and is matched as text, not read as flags. As flags uv would not do either: each is given once, and u and v not together. Write a regular expression literal with the flags meant."}]},
